# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# ── READ THIS BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# When `.easignore` exists, EAS Build uses it INSTEAD OF `.gitignore` — not in
# addition to it. That is the trap this file fell into: it listed six entries, so
# every exclusion `.gitignore` provides was silently switched off and the project
# archive came out at 621 MB. Compressing it took 51 s and uploading it another
# 51 s, on every single build.
#
# Measured contents of that archive:
#
#     422 MB   SF-Symbols-8 (1).dmg          an Apple design-tool installer
#     220 MB   workers/                      the Cloudflare Worker + its own deps
#     160 MB   pixel_characters_pack*.zip    source art, packed
#      27 MB   telegram_ios_settings_icon_pack*.zip
#
# None of it is needed to compile the app. With the rules below the archive is a
# couple of dozen MB.
#
# So: anything added here must be something the BUILD does not read. If a file is
# imported by app code or referenced from app.json, it must NOT be listed.

# ── DO NOT EXCLUDE package-lock.json ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# It was excluded here for one build, to dodge `npm ci`. That works — eas-build picks its
# installer by looking for a lock file — but it picks YARN when there is no npm lock, and
# yarn is strictly worse here:
#
#     Running "yarn install --frozen-lockfile --production false"
#     info No lockfile found.
#     error @supabase/supabase-js@2.112.3: The engine "node" is incompatible with this
#           module. Expected version ">=22.0.0". Got "20.19.4"
#     error Found incompatible module.
#
# yarn treats `engines` as fatal; npm treats it as a warning (and there is no `.npmrc`
# setting `engine-strict`). The builder image runs Node 20.19.4, so any dependency that
# declares `node >= 22` kills a yarn install and is merely noisy under npm.
#
# So the lock STAYS in the archive, npm stays the installer, and the actual `npm ci`
# complaint is fixed at its source instead — see the `@emnapi/*` entries in package.json's
# devDependencies and the comment there.

# ── Secrets and local-only config ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.env.local
credentials.json
build-info.json
.vercel
tokim
AuthKey_*.p8

# ── Agent / editor / planning state ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.agents
.kiro
.vscode
.expo
.github

# ── Backend, deployed separately ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Cloudflare Worker is its own deploy target with its own node_modules; the
# mobile build never imports from it.
workers/
worker/

# ── Design-tool installers and packed source art ────────────────────────────────
# Shipping assets live in assets/ and are referenced from app.json / code. These
# are the ORIGINALS and the tooling, which the build never opens.
*.dmg
*.zip
logoappekpan/
vrii/
targets/

# ── Docs, notes, dumps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/
*.md
!README.md
eple.txt
worker_dump.txt
worker_live_check.txt
build-log.txt
html.txt

# ── Test output and caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
dist/
.jest-cache/
*.log
